Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.1 Conditions to Closing. The obligations of the Acquirer to proceed with the transaction are subject to the following conditions being satisfied or waived: (a) Representations and Warranties. (i) The representations and warranties set forth in Sections 3.1 and 3.2 shall be true and correct in all respects as of the Closing Date, except where the failure to be so true and correct would not have a material adverse effect. (ii) The representations and warranties set forth in Sections 3.3 and 3.4 shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the Closing Date, except where any inaccuracies, individually or in the aggregate, would not reasonably be expected to have a material adverse effect. (iii) Notwithstanding the foregoing, the fundamental representations and warranties shall be deemed accurate if, in the aggregate, they are true and correct to a standard that considers both materiality and the absence of any hybrid adverse effect, as defined in the agreement, as of the Closing Date. (Page 45)\nAnswer:
